I have everything needed. Here is my complete report on the `customerCode` owner-identity code.

# Owner Identity — File Inventory and Code

## Important finding up front: a pending redesign + an existing inconsistency

`src/test/java/.../acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` carries a `global-id` redesign directive at the top and its one test already asserts a **NEW** customerCode format that the current main code does **not** produce:

- Test expects `<REGION>-<HASH8>` matching regex `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`.
- Current `AssignCustomerCode` produces `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007`).
- The OpenAPI doc (`openapi.yml`) describes yet a third format `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (e.g. `SMI-0007`) — its javadoc/doc and the actual code already disagree about whether a CITY3 segment is present.

So there are three different notions of `customerCode` format across test / code / API doc.

---

## 1. `AssignCustomerCode` — how customerCode is currently built

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`

Format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`; NNNN is a **per-city** 4-digit sequence = 1 + count of existing owners in the same city. Runs after `BuildOwner`, before `SaveOwner`.

```java
public class AssignCustomerCode {

    public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        String city = owner.getCity();
        String lastName = owner.getLastName();
        String cityPrefix = prefix(city);
        String lastPrefix = prefix(lastName);
        long sequence = 1L;
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (equalsIgnoreCase(city, existing.getCity())) {
                sequence++;
            }
        }
        owner.setCustomerCode(String.format("%s-%s-%04d", cityPrefix, lastPrefix, sequence));
    }

    private static String prefix(String value) {
        String source = (value == null ? "" : value);
        return source.substring(0, Math.min(3, source.length())).toUpperCase();
    }

    private static boolean equalsIgnoreCase(String a, String b) {
        return a == null ? b == null : a.equalsIgnoreCase(b);
    }
}
```
Note: the class javadoc says the sequence is "per-city", but the OpenAPI doc calls NNNN "a global 4-digit ... sequence". Another code/doc mismatch.

---

## 2. `CheckDigit` — how the check digit is derived

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/CheckDigit.java`

Single Luhn check digit (0–9) over the digits contained in `customerCode`; null when no customerCode.

```java
public final class CheckDigit {

    private CheckDigit() {
    }

    /** The Luhn check digit for the given owner, or null when it has no customer code. */
    public static Integer of(Owner owner) {
        String customerCode = owner.getCustomerCode();
        if (customerCode == null) {
            return null;
        }
        int sum = 0;
        boolean dbl = true;
        for (int i = customerCode.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            char c = customerCode.charAt(i);
            if (c < '0' || c > '9') {
                continue;
            }
            int d = c - '0';
            if (dbl) {
                d *= 2;
                if (d > 9) {
                    d -= 9;
                }
            }
            sum += d;
            dbl = !dbl;
        }
        return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
    }
}
```

---

## 3. Membership number — derived in the mapper (no dedicated class)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

The membershipNumber, checkDigit, membershipLevel, locality and identityKey are all derived via MapStruct `@Mapping` expressions on `toOwnerDto`. Membership number = `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where YY is `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, zero-padded to 2 digits; null when customerCode or registrationDate is null.

```java
@Mapper(uses = PetMapper.class)
public interface OwnerMapper {

    @Mapping(target = "displayName", expression = "java(owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName())")
    @Mapping(target = "initials", expression = "java(owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\")")
    @Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.CheckDigit.of(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "membershipNumber", expression = "java(owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null ? null : owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))")
    @Mapping(target = "membershipLevel", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.MembershipLevel.of(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "locality", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Locality.of(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode()))")
    @Mapping(target = "contactPreference", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.ContactPreference.of(owner))")
    @Mapping(target = "identityKey", expression = "java(org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.IdentityKey.of(owner))")
    OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);
    ...
}
```

The YY segment depends on `registrationDate`, which is rolled to a business day at build time (see BuildOwner/BusinessDay below).

---

## 4. `MembershipLevel`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/MembershipLevel.java`

Starts at 1; +1 if email present; +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`; capped at 3 (`MAX`).

```java
public final class MembershipLevel {

    public static final int MAX = 3;

    private MembershipLevel() {
    }

    public static int of(Owner owner) {
        int level = 1;
        if (owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty()) {
            level++;
        }
        if (owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0) {
            level++;
        }
        return Math.min(level, MAX);
    }
}
```

---

## 5. `AuditOwnerCreated` — the create audit record

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`

Emits an AUDIT-logger line after `SaveOwner`, carrying id, customerCode, registrationDate and membershipLevel.

```java
public class AuditOwnerCreated {

    private static final Logger audit = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");

    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
        audit.info("Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
                owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
                org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.MembershipLevel.of(owner));
    }
