```

---

## 6. `Locality` — how locality/region is derived

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Locality.java`

Prefers postcode range (NSW 2000–2099, VIC 3000–3099, QLD 4000–4099), falling back to a city→region table (Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD); `UNKNOWN` otherwise. Note the mapper calls the two-arg `of(city, postcode)`.

```java
public final class Locality {

    private static final Pattern FOUR_DIGITS = Pattern.compile("^[0-9]{4}$");

    private static final Map<String, String> CITY_REGION = Map.of(
            "Sydney", "NSW", "Melbourne", "VIC", "Brisbane", "QLD");

    private static final Map<String, int[]> REGION_RANGE = Map.of(
            "NSW", new int[] {2000, 2099}, "VIC", new int[] {3000, 3099}, "QLD", new int[] {4000, 4099});

    public static final String UNKNOWN = "UNKNOWN";

    private Locality() {
    }

    public static String of(String city) {
        if (city == null) {
            return UNKNOWN;
        }
        return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(city, UNKNOWN);
    }

    public static String of(String city, String postcode) {
        String byPostcode = fromPostcode(postcode);
        if (!UNKNOWN.equals(byPostcode)) {
            return byPostcode;
        }
        return of(city);
    }

    private static String fromPostcode(String postcode) {
        if (postcode == null || !FOUR_DIGITS.matcher(postcode).matches()) {
            return UNKNOWN;
        }
        int value = Integer.parseInt(postcode);
        for (Map.Entry<String, int[]> entry : REGION_RANGE.entrySet()) {
            int[] range = entry.getValue();
            if (value >= range[0] && value <= range[1]) {
                return entry.getKey();
            }
        }
        return UNKNOWN;
    }
}
```

Note: The OpenAPI doc for `locality` describes only the city-table derivation (`Sydney->NSW...`, `UNKNOWN` when city not in table) and does not mention the postcode-range preference the code actually applies — another doc/code drift.

---

## 7. `Postcode` — postcode validation against region ranges

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Postcode.java`

```java
public final class Postcode {

    private static final Pattern FOUR_DIGITS = Pattern.compile("^[0-9]{4}$");

    private static final Map<String, int[]> REGION_RANGE = Map.of(
            "NSW", new int[] {2000, 2099}, "VIC", new int[] {3000, 3099}, "QLD", new int[] {4000, 4099});

    private Postcode() {
    }

    public static boolean isValidForCity(String postcode, String city) {
        if (postcode == null || !FOUR_DIGITS.matcher(postcode).matches()) {
            return false;
        }
        int[] range = REGION_RANGE.get(Locality.of(city));
        if (range == null) {
            return true;
        }
        int value = Integer.parseInt(postcode);
        return value >= range[0] && value <= range[1];
    }
}
```

